# --- For GitHub Pages / Cloudflare Pages (static hosting) ---
#
# There is no Node/Express server on either platform, so a plain
# GEMINI_API_KEY env var (server-side) can no longer be injected at
# runtime the way AI Studio did it. You have two options:
#
# OPTION A — client-side key (simplest, works on GitHub Pages too)
# Vite only exposes env vars prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.
# Anyone can extract this key from your shipped JS, so only use an
# API key that is restricted (HTTP referrer restrictions / limited
# quota) in Google AI Studio / Google Cloud console.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# OPTION B — Cloudflare Pages Function proxy (recommended, keeps the key
# secret server-side). Only works if you deploy on Cloudflare Pages, not
# GitHub Pages. Set this as a secret in the Cloudflare Pages dashboard
# (Settings → Environment variables), NOT in this file:
# GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"
# See functions/api/gemini.ts for the proxy implementation.

# APP_URL is no longer needed — static hosts don't have a Cloud Run URL.
# If your code references it, replace with the actual deployed URL or
# window.location.origin.
